  "task": {
    "objective": "Use six finite parts to satisfy three chassis-plus-coil orders, reworking defects and matching requested coil colors, then physically carry valid products to the dock before their role-linked deadlines when possible.",
    "natural_termination": "All three product statuses are resolved as shipped (2) or rejected (3). Rejected orders are permanent negative outcomes. Ready but undelivered products do not count as completion. Otherwise truncate at 144 live transitions.",
    "interaction": "Routing, braking and occupied conveyor/machine buffers change partners available parts and delays. Inspection or recipe publication changes partner information. Shared power spent on one rework may prevent a different repair. Assembly permanently consumes two finite parts, and poor hidden-quality decisions impose shared losses.",
    "observation_access": "Partial native information with public geometry, positions, buffers, custody, processing, order deadlines, visible colors, status and events. The six actual defect bits are visible to role 1 or to everyone after part inspection/rework; requested coil colors are visible to role 2 or after a board publication. Explicit per-record mask rows accompany -1 for unknown bits. Separate quality/recipe entity groups use exactly those masks; the public part/order groups never expose the private attributes."
  },
